# Scripts that get embedded and shipped to a RHEL host must keep LF endings on
# every platform.
#
# internal/monitor/pcapd.sh is embedded with //go:embed and shipped as base64; a
# single CR would break its shebang and every line of it. internal/monitor/
# logfilter.awk is uploaded and run with `awk -f`, where a CR ends up inside every
# regex and comparison. Both launch paths normalise endings defensively, but with
# core.autocrlf=true a Windows clone would still check them out as CRLF and fail
# their invariant tests, so pin them here.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.awk text eol=lf
